/P 205 0 R
/E (The Economic Recovery Act of 1948 was signed by President Truman on April 3, 1948. This would become known as the Marshall Plan, named after Secretary of State George Marshall who proposed that the United States should provide economic backing to aid reconstruction in postwar Europe while blocking the expansion of the communist sphere of influence. The Cold War blurred the lines of aid, turning it into a primary weapon and tool of containment as well as geopolitical influence. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
