/E (In 2000, the United Nations established The Millennium Development Goals \(MDGs\), which were eight international development goals aimed at eradicating extreme poverty, improving health, education, and sustainability by 2015. They focused on quantifiable social outcomes, such as halving extreme poverty and reducing child mortality, with most targets compared against 1990 levels. )
