476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (Fiscal substitution is one of the most cited mechanisms of dependency because it alters the fundamental relationship between a state and its revenue sources, including its citizens. When foreign aid becomes a significant component of the national budget, and is thought to be predictable and reliable, it leads to a decline in tax effort. Over time, the state's fiscal institutions atrophy, leaving the government structurally incapable of funding itself without continued external assistance. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 213 0 R
/E (10.2. Aid Fragmentation  )
